.TH DOODLE 1
.SH NAME
doodle \- straight-line drawing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/doodle
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Doodle
is a rubber-band straight-line drawing program,
a port of the TempleOS Demo/Graphics/Doodle.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Pressing button 1 anchors a line; while the button is held
a preview of the straight line from the anchor to the cursor
follows the pointer, and releasing the button commits one
thick straight segment in the current color.
Button 2 (on release) opens a 16-color picker:
click a swatch to choose the drawing color,
or click elsewhere (or press Esc) to cancel and keep the current color.
The drawing starts on a white canvas with black ink.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF space
.TP
.B LMB drag
Rubber-band a straight line; release to commit it
.TP
.B RMB
Open the 16-color picker
.TP
.B any key
Quit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/doodle.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
.SH BUGS
The original runs fullscreen and borderless; this is a normal window.
The original previews the rubber-band line by XOR;
here it is redrawn from a backing image in the chosen color.
